    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe codebase already had a partial `sharesHousehold` feature (the create endpoint *skipped* the duplicate-household conflict when the flag was set). The change was to make it also **assign a stable shared `householdId`** and return it.\n\n**New behavior:** when `POST /api/owners` is called with `sharesHousehold: true` and an existing same-last-name owner already occupies that address, the new owner and every existing member of that household are assigned one stable, shared `householdId`, which is then returned on the owner.\n\n### Changes\n\n- **`HouseholdIdGenerator`** (new component, `service/`) \u2014 single responsibility: derive a stable, shared household identifier from a last name + address. It normalizes both (trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case) and hashes them (SHA-256 \u2192 `HH-<12 hex>`), so any two owners in the same household deterministically map to the same id, independently and across requests. Mirrors the existing `CustomerCodeGenerator` style.\n\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 injected the generator and centralized the normalization there (removed the now-duplicate private `normalizeIdentity`). Added a private `householdMembers(...)` helper reused by both:\n  - `existsOwnerByLastNameAndAddress` (the conflict check) \u2014 now expressed via `householdMembers`.\n  - `shareHousehold(owner)` (new, `@Transactional`) \u2014 computes the shared id, backfills it onto existing members that lack it, sets it on the new owner, and returns it.\n\n- **`ClinicService`** \u2014 declared the new `shareHousehold` method.\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 on create, when `sharesHousehold` is true it calls `clinicService.shareHousehold(owner)` before saving (each request still takes exactly one path \u2014 conflict check *or* household join).\n\n- **`Owner` model** \u2014 added the `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with accessors.\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema, so it's mapped (MapStruct auto-maps it) and returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n- **Schema DDL** \u2014 added the `household_id` column to all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` and the full suite are green.",
